Third-party components bundled in the application package
应用包内置的第三方组件

The BSD 3-Clause license above covers the OHSidian source code and this
project's own glue code. It does NOT relicense the components below: each keeps
its own copyright and license. Full license texts travel with the application
under resources/resfile/pandoc/ together with PANDOC-SOURCE.txt, which pins the
exact versions, npm tarball sha256 values and upstream source URLs.

1. Pandoc (conversion engine, built to WebAssembly)
   - Version: 3.10 (shipped as pandoc.wasm, gzipped as pandoc.wasm.gz)
   - License: GPL-2.0-or-later (GNU General Public License, version 2 or later)
   - Copyright (C) 2006-2024 John MacFarlane <jgm at berkeley dot edu> and the
     Pandoc contributors. Pandoc embeds some third-party code under
     GPL-compatible licenses; see the COPYRIGHT file of the Pandoc source.
   - Full license text in the package:
     resources/resfile/pandoc/LICENSE-GPL-2.0.txt
     resources/resfile/pandoc/LICENSE-pandoc-wasm.txt
   - Corresponding source (preferred form for modification):
     https://hackage.haskell.org/package/pandoc-3.10/pandoc-3.10.tar.gz
     https://github.com/jgm/pandoc/tree/3.10

2. pandoc-wasm (JavaScript WebAssembly loader bundled into pandoc-service.cjs)
   - Version: 1.1.0
   - License: MIT
   - Copyright (c) Tweag I/O Limited, Johannes Wilm, and pandoc-wasm
     contributors.
   - Source: https://registry.npmjs.org/pandoc-wasm/-/pandoc-wasm-1.1.0.tgz
     (sha256 693bf76c2365254378500a2370a5995ebeb5f859248784ea827eb687878614a2)
     https://github.com/pandoc/pandoc-wasm

3. browser_wasi_shim (WASI runtime shim bundled into pandoc-service.cjs)
   - Version: 0.4.2
   - License: MIT OR Apache-2.0 (this application complies under the MIT option)
   - Copyright (c) bjorn3 and browser_wasi_shim contributors.
   - Full MIT text in the package:
     resources/resfile/pandoc/LICENSE-browser-wasi-shim.txt
   - Source: https://registry.npmjs.org/@bjorn3/browser_wasi_shim/-/browser_wasi_shim-0.4.2.tgz
     (sha256 9c0281520d0e99f027ec7c1c79b4036c0f8168ed9bf98aba19db4737a1333782)
     https://github.com/bjorn3/browser_wasi_shim

4. Build-time-only tools (NOT distributed in the application package)
   - esbuild (MIT), @electron/asar (MIT).

Source-availability statement (GPL-2.0 section 3)
The complete corresponding source code for the GPL-covered Pandoc engine is
available at the exact versions and URLs listed above, and the package is
reproducible from them with the public build script
(scripts/build-pandoc-wasm.mjs) plus the sha256 values pinned in
scripts/pandoc-wasm.lock.json. A written offer for a machine-readable copy of
the corresponding source can be requested at
https://github.com/PCFXPCFX/OHSidian/issues and remains valid for at least
three years from the release date. The GPL-covered engine is a separate,
self-contained component: it is loaded from its own files and, on devices where
the renderer has no WebAssembly, executed in a separate utility process (see
docs/PLATFORM-ADAPTATION.md section 6.11). The component is bundled inside the
application package - users are never asked to download it.

